To install OpenCalcOS (OCOS) on your TI-Nspire CX calculator with TI-Nspire OS firmware versions 3.6 to 6.4.0.74, you need to follow these steps:

1) Install NDless to run other programs:

==> For version: 3.6

Place the ndless_installer.tns and ndless_resources.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer.tns. Wait for the message that NDless has been installed successfully.

==> For version: 3.9.0

Place the ndless_installer_3.9.0_classic_new.tns and ndless_resources.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer.tns. Wait for the message that NDless has been installed successfully, then press Ctrl+W to exit. Successfully installed

==> For version: 3.9.1

Place the ndless_installer_3.9.1.tns and ndless_resources.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, disconnect the USB data cable, then run ndless_installer_3.9.1.tns, and wait for NDless to install.

==> For version: 4.0.3

Place the ndless_installer_4.0.3_cx.tns and ndless_installer.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer_4.0.3_cx.tns. Wait for the message that NDless has been installed successfully, then press Ctrl+W to exit.

==> For version: 4.2.0

Place the ndless_installer_4.2.0_cx.tns and ndless_installer.tns files in ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer_4.2.0_cx.tns. Wait for the message that NDless has been installed successfully, then press Ctrl+W to exit.

==> For version: 4.4.0

Place the ndless_installer_4.4.0.tns and ndless_installer.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer_4.4.0.tns. Wait for the message that NDless has been installed successfully, then press Ctrl+W to exit.

==> For version: 4.5.0

Place the ndless_installer_4.5.0.tns and ndless_installer.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer_4.5.0.tns. Wait for the message that NDless has been installed successfully, then press Ctrl+W to exit. Exit

==> For version: 4.5.3.14 + 4.5.4.48

Place the ndless_installer_4.5.3-4.5.4.tns and ndless_installer.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer_4.5.3-4.5.4.tns. Wait for the message that NDless was installed successfully.

==> For version: 5.2.0.771 + 5.3.0.564

Place the ndless_installer_5.2.0-5.3.0.tns and ndless_installer.tns files in the ndless folder on your calculator, and run ndless_installer_5.2.0-5.3.0.tns. Wait for the message that NDless was installed successfully.

==> For version: 4.5.5.79

Set your language to English through the Settings menu
Press [Home] > [5] (Settings) > [1] (Change Language) -> English
Determine your "boot1" version (needed later).
Press [Home] > [5] (Settings) > [4] (Status) > About button.
Here is a YouTube video for this.
Transfer ndless_installer_4.5.5-6.2.0-6.4.0.tns into a folder named "ndless" (top-level)
Transfer ndless_resources.tns into the same folder
Open the installer, press the corresponding key for your boot1 version and wait
If it fails or reboots, try again until it works

==> For version: 6.2.0.333 + 6.4.0.74

Set your language to English through the Settings menu
Press [Home] > [5] (Settings) > [1] (Change Language) -> English
Transfer ndless_installer_4.5.5-6.2.0-6.4.0.tns into a folder named "ndless" (top-level)
Transfer ndless_resources.tns into the same folder
Open the installer, press any alphanumeric key and wait
If it fails or reboots, try Again until it works

2) After you've installed NDless, you need to download the latest version of OCOS to your calculator. To do this, follow these steps:

==> Installing OCOS

You currently have the files zCalc.tns, CalcFS.tns, and Loader.tns in this folder. You need to place all of these files in the OCOS folder:

Create a "OCOS" folder on your calculator and place the following files in this folder:

- zCalc.tns - Beep kernel
- CalcFS.tns - Temporary file system with Init and a ready-made system for the Beep kernel
- Loader.tns - Loads zCalc.tns and CalcFS.tns into RAM and runs zCalc.tns, specifying the Calc file system unpacked into RAM.

==> Launching

Once all the files have been placed, run Loader.tns. It will successfully load the entire system, and you'll be in OCOS!

Good luck with installing and using OCOS!
